-- std.compiler.host — SH-03's production-dispatch anchor.
--
-- WHY THIS MODULE EXISTS. Deleting it as a no-op wrapper breaks the C ABI, so
-- the reason is recorded here rather than in a commit message.
--
-- `--lib` emits an `__attribute__((constructor))` that runs the runtime's
-- initializers and `duo_register_modules()`. That registration initializes
-- every REQUIRED module. It does not initialize the module being compiled:
-- a primary module's file-scope bindings are emitted as statements inside
-- `main`, and `--lib` never emits `main`. So the top module of a library
-- artifact is the one module that is never initialized. Measured — see
-- gaps/GAP-020.md for the four-line repro.
--
-- lib/std/compiler/lexer.duo has file-scope state, so compiling it directly as
-- the artifact yields exports that dereference NULL. Compiling THIS module
-- instead demotes the lexer to a dependency, which is the path that already
-- works, and the lexer's own flat symbols — duo_lexer_tokenize_all,
-- duo_lexer_step, duo_lexer_text_fingerprint — become callable unchanged.
--
--     duo compile lib/std/compiler/host.duo --backend=c --lib --emit obj
--
-- The host ABI is therefore the lexer's, not this module's. What is added here
-- is only what a foreign caller cannot otherwise ask: the record layout it is
-- about to decode, and a self-test that the boundary is live.
--
-- The ambient reference below is load-bearing. It is what puts the lexer on the
-- registration path; an unreferenced module is not linked in.

-- Bytes per token written by `duo_lexer_tokenize_all`, as i64 slots:
-- kind, loc.line, loc.col, int_val. A host decoding the buffer should assert
-- this rather than hard-code 4, so a layout change fails loudly at the seam.
@c.export("duo_lexer_host_stride")
duo_lexer_host_stride(): i64
    4
end

-- One call that proves the boundary is initialized. Returns the token count
-- for a fixed source, so a host can distinguish "linked and live" from "linked
-- and reading uninitialized state" without knowing any Duo.
@c.export("duo_lexer_host_probe")
duo_lexer_host_probe(out: i64, cap: i64): i64
    std.compiler.lexer.duo_lexer_tokenize_all("fun add(a: i64): i64 = a + 1 end",
        "probe.duo", out, cap)
end
